From 0a53fe06ec26c32207f3394083df43c01a2a2912 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenSec <contactus@opensec.in>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:04:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AOT: x86-64 back end and runtime improvements for
 ahead-of-time code

Ports the ahead-of-time (AOT) compiler of oven-sh/WebKit's AOT branch,
which had ARM64 stubs only, to Linux x86-64, and improves what compiled
programs spend their time on.

x86-64 back end
- aot/AOTStubsX86_64.cpp: the stub layer (calls, property and element access,
  polymorphic and megamorphic caches, scopes, arithmetic and comparisons,
  allocation front ends and helpers, call intrinsics including Map/Set,
  bound-function calls), with C-convention adapters and RIP-relative linking.
- Stubs on the hot path keep to caller-saved registers ("light" stubs), so
  compiled code can keep values in rbx/r12 across them (useAOTLightStubs).
- Image code for regular expressions on x86-64, including unicode patterns:
  the surrogate-pair slow path is emitted into the pattern's own code.
- Inline double-to-int32 for bit operations; frame pointers kept.

Compiler
- Inline polymorphic property reads in loops (4-entry probe) and the
  out-of-line/holder cases of monomorphic reads.
- Verbose inlining diagnostics (AOT-INLINE) for builds with
  verboseAOTCompilation.

Runtime
- RegExp first-code-unit prefilter: patterns whose matches start with a rare
  code unit (lone-surrogate stripping, CJK/Thai sanitizers) skip ahead with
  SIMD and fail at once on Latin-1 subjects.
- aotRecordRegExpsPath / aotRegExpsPath: regular expressions a program builds
  at run time are recorded and compiled into the image like literals.
- Image regexps may lack 16-bit code; such subjects fall back to the
  interpreter, and only when the regexp JIT is off.
- BumpPointerPool grows geometrically (the Yarr interpreter no longer maps and
  unmaps pages around every match).
- Realms other than the program's reserve their AOT instance without
  committing it; memory becomes writable as it is used.
- StaticRegion reserves what the address space allows and reports it, so an
  embedder can decline the static heap under ulimit -v or strict overcommit.
- Fixes: far calls from JIT code into an image, image code in a second VM,
  callee-save handling of tail calls.
